From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:17:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: terrain textures wrap with GL_REPEAT

swrast draws a textured triangle through its fast integer path
(persp_textured_triangle) only when the texture has one level in use,
the same min and mag filter, and GL_REPEAT wrapping. The terrain pages
used GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE, so every terrain pixel went through the general
per-fragment path (fetch_texel_2d, lerp_rgba_2d, linear_texel_locations:
two thirds of the frame). With GL_REPEAT, and the "fast" or "nearest"
filter, the terrain takes the fast path: CAM_1A at 800x600 goes from 30
to 51 fps on the profiling host. The picture is the same apart from
rounding (at most 2/255 per channel); the wrap mode only changes the
outer half texel of each page.
---
 src/texture.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/texture.c b/src/texture.c
index e844a10..f5dc3f5 100644
--- a/src/texture.c
+++ b/src/texture.c
@@ -111,8 +111,18 @@ static int newPage(const char *name, int level, int width, int height, int count
 	             GL_RGBA, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, NULL);
 	glTexEnvf(GL_TEXTURE_ENV, GL_TEXTURE_ENV_MODE, GL_MODULATE);
 	pie_Set3DTextureFilter();
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+	// Software OpenGL only has a fast path for textured triangles with
+	// GL_REPEAT (swrast's persp_textured_triangle); anything else samples
+	// each pixel through the general code, at half the frame rate. The
+	// wrap mode only affects the outer half texel of a page, and tiles
+	// already blend into their neighbours inside the page.
+	glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_WRAP_S, GL_REPEAT);
+	glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_WRAP_T, GL_REPEAT);
+#else
 	glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_WRAP_S, GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
 	glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_WRAP_T, GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
+#endif
 
 	return texPage;
 }
